---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CallToAction from '../../components/CallToAction.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Selling a Home in the Wichita Area | Charity Menefee"
  description="Thoughtful guidance for preparing and selling a home in Wichita and nearby communities."
>
  <div class="buying-page selling-page">
    <PageHero
      eyebrow="Selling roadmap"
      title="Selling your home, one decision at a time."
      intro="Selling a home can feel like a long list of decisions. It gets easier when you take them in the right order. Here's how I'll help you work through preparation, the market, and the path to closing."
    />

    <section class="buying-roadmap-section selling-roadmap-section" aria-label="Home-selling roadmap">
      <ol class="shell buying-roadmap selling-roadmap">
        <li class="buying-stage selling-stage" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number selling-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body selling-stage-body" aria-labelledby="selling-step-one-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading selling-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Before the sign goes in the yard</p>
              <h2 id="selling-step-one-title">Start with the big picture.</h2>
              <p>Before thinking about paint colors, photography, or price, get clear about what the sale needs to accomplish.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details selling-stage-details">
              <p class="buying-list-intro">Begin with the practical questions:</p>
              <ul class="buying-checklist">
                <li>Your ideal timing and reason for selling</li>
                <li>What needs to happen after the sale</li>
                <li>Whether another purchase or move is involved</li>
                <li>The property's current condition</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll help organize those priorities into a workable starting plan.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage selling-stage selling-stage-prep" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number selling-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body selling-stage-body" aria-labelledby="selling-step-two-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading selling-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Prepare without overdoing it</p>
              <h2 id="selling-step-two-title">Decide what is worth doing.</h2>
              <p>Good preparation doesn't mean remodeling everything. The useful work depends on the property, its condition, and your timing. An established Wichita home may need different preparation than newer construction or acreage.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details selling-stage-details">
              <div class="selling-prep-grid">
                <section class="selling-prep-panel selling-prep-panel-worth" aria-labelledby="selling-worth-title">
                  <h3 id="selling-worth-title">Worth looking at</h3>
                  <ul class="buying-checklist">
                    <li>Obvious maintenance issues</li>
                    <li>Cleaning and decluttering</li>
                    <li>Small repairs and curb appeal</li>
                    <li>Anything likely to distract buyers</li>
                  </ul>
                </section>
                <section class="selling-prep-panel selling-prep-panel-caution" aria-labelledby="selling-caution-title">
                  <h3 id="selling-caution-title">Think twice before</h3>
                  <ul class="buying-checklist">
                    <li>Expensive renovations</li>
                    <li>Highly personal upgrades</li>
                    <li>Projects based only on assumed requirements</li>
                  </ul>
                </section>
              </div>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll help you compare the effort, timing, and likely usefulness of each option without promising that a project will increase value.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage selling-stage selling-stage-market" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number selling-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body selling-stage-body" aria-labelledby="selling-step-three-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading selling-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Getting ready for the market</p>
              <h2 id="selling-step-three-title">Price and present the home.</h2>
              <p>After we decide what to do before listing, we'll work through the price and get the home ready to make a good first impression.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details selling-stage-details selling-market-details">
              <div class="selling-market-group">
                <h3>Pricing considerations</h3>
                <ul class="buying-checklist selling-market-list">
                  <li>Comparable properties and current competition</li>
                  <li>Condition, location, and property features</li>
                  <li>The market context at the time of listing</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div class="selling-market-group">
                <h3>Getting ready to list</h3>
                <ul class="buying-checklist selling-market-list">
                  <li>Making sure your home is ready for photos</li>
                  <li>Preparing for showings and making it easy for buyers to visit</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll pull and review comparable properties (comps), talk through what they tell us about your home, and help choose a pricing position that makes sense for the market.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage buying-stage-offer selling-stage selling-stage-offers" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number selling-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body selling-stage-body" aria-labelledby="selling-step-four-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading selling-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Once buyers enter the picture</p>
              <h2 id="selling-step-four-title">Handle showings, offers, and decisions.</h2>
              <p>This stage brings new information quickly. I'll keep the details organized so you can compare what each option means for your plans.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details selling-stage-details">
              <div class="buying-decision-grid selling-decision-grid">
                <section aria-labelledby="selling-showings-title">
                  <h3 id="selling-showings-title">Showings</h3>
                  <p>Make it easy for buyers to see your home, keep it ready to show, and use their feedback when it's helpful.</p>
                </section>
                <section aria-labelledby="selling-offers-title">
                  <h3 id="selling-offers-title">Offers</h3>
                  <p>Review price alongside financing, timing, contingencies, concessions, and other terms.</p>
                </section>
                <section aria-labelledby="selling-decisions-title">
                  <h3 id="selling-decisions-title">Decisions</h3>
                  <p>Compare the whole proposal. The highest offer isn't automatically the strongest fit.</p>
                </section>
              </div>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll help you understand the options, talk through the pros and cons, and answer questions along the way, but the final decision is always yours.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>

        <li class="buying-stage buying-stage-closing selling-stage selling-stage-closing" data-reveal="up">
          <span class="buying-stage-number selling-stage-number" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <article class="buying-stage-body selling-stage-body" aria-labelledby="selling-step-five-title">
            <div class="buying-stage-heading selling-stage-heading">
              <p class="eyebrow">Finishing the sale</p>
              <h2 id="selling-step-five-title">Move from contract to closing.</h2>
              <p>An accepted offer begins the final phase rather than ending the work. The exact path depends on the agreement and the property.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="buying-stage-details selling-stage-details">
              <ul class="buying-checklist selling-closing-list">
                <li>Inspections and repair discussions when applicable</li>
                <li>Appraisal when the buyer's financing requires one</li>
                <li>Title and closing coordination</li>
                <li>Possession planning and the final handoff</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="buying-stage-note">I'll keep an eye on deadlines, coordinate with everyone involved, and help keep things moving through closing.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <CallToAction
      title="Thinking about selling?"
      copy="Not sure what your home needs first? Tell me what you're considering, and I'll help you figure out a practical next step."
    />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
